 # Quadric SDF (First-Order Approximation)
 ## Overview
-Computes an approximate signed distance from a query point to a quadric surface defined by a general quadratic equation, using a first-order Taylor approximation [S1, unofficial]. It enables ray marching against arbitrary quadrics (ellipsoids, hyperboloids, paraboloids) without deriving closed-form distance functions, trading geometric accuracy for implementation simplicity [S1, unofficial]. Unlike exact SDF primitives [SDF Primitives](1731-sdf-primitives.md), it provides a bound rather than the true distance, which may cause jitter or missed collisions if the gradient is small.
